share_shrink":65.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0026818095056308456,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":95.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.0028900001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["flagged"],"description_full":"Target Corporation operates as a general merchandise retailer in the United States. It offers apparel for women, men, young adults, kids, toddlers, and babies, as well as jewelry, accessories, and shoes; and beauty products, such as skin and bath care, cosmetics, hair care, oral care, deodorant, and shaving products. The company also provides food and beverage products comprising dry and perishable grocery, including snacks, candy, beverages, deli, bakery, meat, produce, and food service; electronics which includes video games and consoles, toys, sporting goods, entertainment, and luggage; bed and bath, home d\u00e9cor, school/office supplies, storage, small appliances, kitchenware, greeting cards, party supplies, furniture, lighting, home improvement, and seasonal merchandise; and household essentials, such as household cleaning, paper products, over-the-counter healthcare, vitamins and supplements, baby gear, and pet supplies. In addition, it sells merchandise through periodic design and creative partnerships, and shop-in-shop experience; and in-store amenities. The company sells its products through its stores; and digital channels, including Target.com. Target Corporation was incorporated in 1902 and is headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael J. Fiddelke | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 400K people. Revenue per employee of $262K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $7K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $702 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Target Corporation is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $77.9B market cap on $104.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 8% cost of capital, a 10-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 29%.","The business throws off $2.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 47% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4672873049852801},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $27.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["42 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Target (TGT) Chair Sold Shares. How Much Do They Still Hold?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-retailing/nyse-tgt/target/news/the-target-tgt-chair-sold-shares-how-much-do-they-still-hold","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795767191.661,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Skip the Doorbusters, Collect the Dividends: $90,000 in Target, Macy\u2019s, and Best Buy Pays $2,885 a Year","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/skip-doorbusters-collect-dividends-90-213405960.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795815245.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.881,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Target\u2019s Former CEO Just Sold $4.4 Million of Stock Heading Into Black Friday","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/target-former-ceo-just-sold-150834216.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795792114.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":1,"scope":"comp